            "design": "Retrospective cohort study using deidentified electronic health record data from six academic medical centers within the University of California Health system.",
            "exposure_definition": "Antibiotic exposure windows categorized as pre-only (-60 to -1 days), post-only (+1 to +60 days), both windows, or none. Included systemic oral/IV antibiotics with known microbiome impact (penicillins, cephalosporins, carbapenems, fluoroquinolones, macrolides, tetracyclines, sulfonamides, metronidazole, clindamycin, vancomycin, linezolid). Required >=2 distinct days of administration.",
