        "material_ready": true,
        "material_usefulness": "supporting",
        "outline_action": "Search for published results from the CanBiome2 trial (NCT06623461) or other large-scale randomized phase III trials of microbiome interventions in ICI-treated cancer patients to determine if any have been completed and reported since this publication.",
        "outline_action_recovered_by_policy": false,
        "remaining_gap": "The gap requires evidence of a completed large randomised phase III trial. This material provides only a phase 2 trial. While the authors reference an ongoing/forthcoming phase 3 trial (CanBiome2), they do not provide its results or confirm its completion within this text.",
        "remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy": false,
        "status": "unmet",
        "useful_material": "This study reports the results of FMT-LUMINate, a multicenter, open-label, phase 2 trial evaluating healthy donor fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) combined with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) in patients with non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) or melanoma. The trial enrolled 40 patients (20 NSCLC, 20 melanoma). In the NSCLC cohort receiving anti-PD-1 monotherapy, the objective response rate (ORR) was 80%. In the melanoma cohort receiving dual anti-PD-1 and anti-CTLA-4 therapy, the ORR was 75%. The study found that clinical response was associated with the loss of baseline deleterious bacterial species rather than the engraftment of donor-specific strains. Safety data indicated no grade 3+ adverse events in the NSCLC cohort, but a higher incidence of severe immune-related adverse events (including myocarditis) in the melanoma cohort, particularly among recipients of donors rich in Prevotella spp."
      },
      "supplement_materials": [
        {
          "auxiliary_material": "The authors explicitly state that this is a phase 2 trial, not a phase 3 trial. They mention that the findings will be assessed as part of the CanBiome2 randomized trial (NCT06623461), which is described as a randomized trial evaluating FMT in combination with ICI in 128 patients, but the current paper does not report the results of this phase 3 trial. The study design was open-label and single-arm for the cohorts reported here, lacking the randomization required for a phase 3 RCT status.",
          "evidence": [],
          "gap_id": "case_E_phase3_rct",
          "judgment_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\progressive_review_plan\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\03_external_closure\\runs\\case_E_phase3_rct\\source_units\\SU01_search_candidate_dcbe39b3d2\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json",
