      "supplement_material": {
        "auxiliary_material": "The study highlights regimen-specific effects, noting that microbial associations with outcomes differed between the PD-1 inhibitor-based regimen (PC) and the dual checkpoint blockade regimen (NIC). It identifies specific bacterial genera (Fusicatenibacter, Butyricicoccus, Blautia) enriched in patients with longer OS (>12 or >18 months). It also notes that lower microbial alpha diversity and presence of certain taxa were linked to a higher risk of serious (≥ Grade 4) AEs. The authors conclude that gut microbiota may serve as a biomarker for chemo-immunotherapy in advanced NSCLC.",
